From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] oleaut32: picture save formats, SaveAsFile, icon sizes, OleSavePictureFile, font SetHdc and property bag

Standard picture:
- Metafile and enhanced metafile pictures could not be saved (FIXMEs):
  a metafile now saves as a placeable metafile with its size in the
  header, an enhanced metafile as its bits; both load again. An
  enhanced metafile picture made from a PICTDESC takes its size from
  the metafile's frame (it was 0 by 0, "EMF is not supported").
- A bitmap loaded from a JPEG, GIF or PNG and changed saves in that
  format again when the original format is kept (FIXMEs); its format is
  remembered past the decoding, which had reset it to BMP.
- GetSizeMax answers for every type (a "partial stub").
- SaveAsFile (a "hacked stub" that wrote whatever data it had) writes
  the file the picture was loaded from, or with fSaveMemCopy a file made
  from the picture in memory; without one and without an original it
  fails with E_FAIL, and an empty picture writes nothing, as Windows
  does (Wine's olepicture tests' todos now pass and are unmarked).
- IsDirty (a stub) answers; EnumConnectionPoints (a stub) enumerates
  the picture's IPropertyNotifySink point; the class factory answers
  QueryInterface and LockServer.
- OleLoadPicture and OleLoadPictureEx make the picture own what it
  loads and set KeepOriginalFormat to the opposite of fRunmode, as
  documented (the handle was not owned with fRunmode TRUE, and
  KeepOriginalFormat was always TRUE). OleLoadPictureEx's size and
  colour flags choose the icon image (the first 32 pixel one was taken
  whatever was asked) and size it.
- OleSavePictureFile (a stub) writes the picture's file.
- OleLoadPicturePath of an empty name answers INET_E_UNKNOWN_PROTOCOL.

Standard font:
- SetHdc (a stub) sizes the font for the DC's mapping mode.
- EnumConnectionPoints (a stub) enumerates its two connection points.
- The property bag's GetClassID and Save (stubs that failed) give
  CLSID_StdFont and write the properties Load reads.

Wine's oleaut32 olepicture (27 todos now pass and are unmarked) and
olefont tests: no failures.

Gate: test/oapict-gate.sh (Xvfb, test/oapict-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_METAFILE_SAVE, SG_MUTANT_ICON_FIRST
(oleaut32/olepicture.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_FONT_BAG (oleaut32/olefont.c).
